From 67403b8d3dffc02d0c1334e67c5cc9698f09e328 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Owen <3221756+christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 17:47:07 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 171/274] DeepSeek V4.1 WO-A's input is prepared once, in the
 attention's output store

The reference prepares WO-A's input after the attention: the trailing RoPE
columns rotated back, then act_quant(o, 32, "ue8m0", inplace=True). 0177 did the
quantization in WO-A's W8A16 GEMM as it loaded each activation tile, so every
column tile of every group redid it: the 1017 release measured prefill 3% and
the decode step 0.7% slower than r6s.

The sparse MLA kernels now do both in their output store, once per row
(sparse_mla.wo_input): extend stages O * (1 / L), rounded to BF16 as before,
in Q_shared; the decode merge in a row of shared memory. The rotation is
rope_'s inverse arithmetic, the quantization _reference_roundtrip, in the same
order and rounding as before, so WO-A's input keeps its bits. The kernels take
the rows' positions and the RoPE table; the layer no longer declares or
launches WO's inverse RoPE, and the GEMM loads its BF16 tiles as it did before
0177.

Tests: wo_input bit for bit against TileKernels' inverse rotation and
per_token_cast, compiled with fast math as the attention is, at the extend and
merge head blocks; the sparse MLA's output against the reference attention
through the same, within one E4M3 step, as act_quant's fixed point and equal on
every route; WO on prepared input.

